# Game Over Ever After was pulled from the site entirely at 906efc9 — no
# local art existed to replace its dead YouTube hero (#61). There's nothing
# to redirect to; send it to the archive listing rather than a bare 404.
/projects/gameOverEverAfter  /projects                      301

# --- Blog: no live blog section by decision (see CLAUDE.md) ----------------
# The 20 posts were scraped to content/archive/ as source material, mined
# into the About narrative and project pages, and never republished as their
# own URLs — there were no per-post permalinks on the old site to begin with,
# only this pagination shell (/blog/, /blog/?offset=N, per .htaccess's
# `RewriteRule ^blog/ - [L,NC]`). _redirects doesn't match query strings, so
# one rule per path form covers every offset. Both the trailing-slash and
# bare forms are listed: unlike /projects/, nothing under /blog/ is a real
# asset, so Cloudflare's drop-trailing-slash asset handling never kicks in to
# normalize one into the other.
/blog                         /about                         301
/blog/                        /about                         301

# --- Stray public files: deliberate 404, not a redirect --------------------
# todo.txt, palette.html, colors.css, and wp-login.php were live at capture
# time but have no honest destination on the new site — todo.txt and
# wp-login.php never had one, and palette.html/colors.css's actual content
# (the old Paletton palette) is discussed in CLAUDE.md's Phase 5 section
# rather than served as a page. Left unlisted on purpose: Cloudflare's
# `not_found_handling: 404-page` already serves the real 404 page for any
# path with no rule and no matching asset, which is the deliberate answer.
